# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   So Takamoto et al. (2022). Towards universal neural network potential for material discovery applicable to arbitrary combination of 45 elements.
#   Nature Communications. doi:10.1038/s41467-022-30687-9  arXiv:2106.14583v2
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2106.14583v2 (sha256 eebf57aebebaf6c8...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 137 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
#
# Encoding scope: the PFP model (TeaNet architecture with modifications,
# trained on the PFP molecule and crystal data sets plus OC20), a PFP
# variant trained on OC20 only, and the HME21 architecture benchmark
# (TeaNet, SchNet, PaiNN, NequIP), with the energy and force errors of the
# supplementary tables. Read from the arXiv preprint (v2).

@prefix rdf: <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .
@prefix schema: <https://schema.org/> .
@prefix mls: <http://www.w3.org/ns/mls#> .
@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .
@prefix mlips: <https://w3id.org/mlips#> .
@prefix entity: <https://w3id.org/mlips/entity/> .

###############################################################################
# Q1 -- Bibliographic identification
###############################################################################

entity:study-takamoto2022pfp a mlips:BenchmarkStudy ;
    rdfs:label "Takamoto et al. (2022): PFP, a universal neural network potential for 45 elements" ;
    mlips:reportedIn entity:article-takamoto2022pfp .

